# Pinned shellcheck for this repository's lint gate.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# ===================
# `.github/scripts/ci/01-lint.sh` runs one shellcheck command, and for a while it ran it
# against whatever version happened to be present: the GitHub runner image shipped 0.9.0
# and a contributor's machine had 0.11.0. Those two disagree — 0.11.0 no longer emits an
# SC2317 "command appears unreachable" false positive for a function invoked by an `EXIT`
# trap, which 0.9.0 still emits. The result was a commit whose local gate exited 0 and
# whose CI went red, and the cause was the checker, not the tree.
#
# A gate whose verdict depends on an unpinned tool is not a gate. This file is the single
# source of truth for which version that is: CI installs exactly this one, and 01-lint.sh
# reads the version from here to tell a contributor when theirs differs. Neither of them
# carries its own copy, because two copies of a version number is how this recurs.
#
# CHOOSING THE VERSION
# ====================
# Pinned forward to 0.11.0 rather than back to the runner image's 0.9.0. Pinning to the
# old default would enshrine the false positive that started this, and 0.11.0 is what a
# contributor on a current machine already has — so the pin moves CI to meet developers
# rather than moving developers back to CI.
#
# BUMPING IT
# ==========
# Change `version`, replace BOTH hashes with the real ones from the release, and run the
# lint gate. Hashes are verified in CI before the binary is used, so a wrong one fails
# the build loudly instead of silently running an unexpected checker. Get them with:
#
#   V=<version>
#   for a in x86_64 aarch64; do
#     curl -sSLf "https://github.com/koalaman/shellcheck/releases/download/v$V/shellcheck-v$V.linux.$a.tar.xz" \
#       | shasum -a 256 | awk -v a="$a" '{print "sha256_"a"="$1}'
#   done
#
# Expect the tree to need fixes when bumping: a newer shellcheck finds more, which is the
# point of bumping. Fix findings at the source; reach for a `disable` directive only when
# the finding is genuinely wrong, and say why on the same line.

version=0.11.0
sha256_x86_64=8c3be12b05d5c177a04c29e3c78ce89ac86f1595681cab149b65b97c4e227198
sha256_aarch64=12b331c1d2db6b9eb13cfca64306b1b157a86eb69db83023e261eaa7e7c14588
